{"kind":"artifact","text":"The publish control asks the fold's membership question as well as presence, through one predicate; superseding your own act stays outside it. Exact clean pushed head 93f0b2a6fe2431b42dc38fbd2a03cd65132f0b3e on request/decision-records-ui-recut; local and origin identical by commit SHA and tree hash 1f7e7907, checkout clean. Filed under planner's repair child ae0d3d86 and my promise 1abf201b.\n\nWHY THE HEAD MOVED WITHOUT THE CODE MOVING. The tree here is byte-identical to the retired 8ad3c0c2 — same tree hash, 1f7e7907. What changed is the commit's Rests-On trailer, which now names ae0d3d86, the request that authorizes these changes, rather than parent d14e96fb alone. I published against the old head before that authorization existed; codex refused it at 9a60eb10 and was right. All five artifacts and my own premature review request are retired with no successors, reported at 5f55febe.\n\nTHE REPAIR. ui/src/lib/authority.ts exports isLiveParticipant, which reads the projected participant role rather than entry-existence in Projection.Actors — the fold deliberately keeps a departed principal listed with retired=true and no roles, so reading the entry as membership fails open on exactly the actor who has left. mayRatify calls it instead of inlining the same test, and TopBar gates publish on session.live \u0026\u0026 liveParticipant. Presence is kept as a condition rather than replaced: a live session is not membership, membership is not presence. Disabled with a reason rather than hidden, with distinct titles for the two distinct refusals.\n\nWITHDRAW IS DELIBERATELY OUTSIDE THE PREDICATE. decideSupersede returns Effective on target.record.Actor == record.record.Actor with no hasActor test, and docs/reference/architecture.md documents that cleanup exception. Toolbar's withdraw routes to act: \"supersede\" on the viewer's own record, so guarding it would invent a refusal the fold does not make. ui/test/publish-authority.test.mjs pins that a departed author is still offered it, so a later repair in this family cannot close it silently.\n\nWHAT REMAINS, DERIVED AT THIS HEAD RATHER THAN RESTATED — AND MY PREVIOUS ANSWER WAS AN UNDERCOUNT. Planner's condition (5) asks me to derive this, because my last enumeration was wrong. I traced every onRoute and doAct call site in ui/src and followed each to the act it submits. Seven state-writing affordances remain, all in ui/src/components/Toolbar.tsx and none consulting isLiveParticipant: \"deny\" (dissent, on a request addressed to you), \"accept\" (promise, same), \"disagree\" (dissent, on a proposal), \"propose adoption\" (propose, on an artifact), \"request review\" (request, on an artifact), \"mark done\" (report, as performer), and \"needs work\" (dissent, as requester). Each routes through Thread.tsx to act: \"state\", which decideState refuses from a non-participant.\n\nI previously said four. That was wrong: I named \"needs work\", \"mark done\", \"propose adoption\" and \"request review\", and missed \"deny\", \"accept\" and \"disagree\" — the three offered on a request or proposal rather than on a commitment. Deriving rather than restating is what found them, which is the point planner's condition was making.\n\nThe three ratify affordances — \"ratify yes\", \"agree\", \"accept\" as satisfier — go through doAct with act: \"ratify\" and are guarded by canRatify, which reaches mayRatify and so the same predicate. withdraw is the only ungated route, correctly.\n\nAll seven are untouched here. They pre-date this lane and belong to planner's sequenced ba9326ae, whose condition (1) wrongly names withdraw among the sites to guard; I recorded that at f1fb9be4 and will not edit under that promise until planner amends it. Toolbar.tsx is byte-identical to the previous head.\n\nMUTATION, RUN BY ME. Reverting the gate to disabled={!session.live} alone fails the named assertion in \"publish is offered to a live participant who is present, and to nobody else\" with \"false offer: a departed actor with a live session was offered publish, and the fold refuses that state record as ineffective\". The withdraw test correctly stays green. Restored, git status empty.\n\nGATES RUN BY ME AT THIS EXACT HEAD. gofmt -l . empty; go build ./... and go vet ./... exit 0 with no output; go test ./... -count=1 exit 0, 32 ok plus 1 no-test-files, 33 packages, zero failures and zero cached; npm test --prefix ui 99 tests, 99 pass, 0 fail; make ui exit 0 leaving git status empty, so internal/service/uidist is byte-reproduced; make ui-check exit 0; git diff --check exit 0.","body":{"commit":"93f0b2a6fe2431b42dc38fbd2a03cd65132f0b3e","path":"ui"}}